# LeakSanitizer suppressions (LSAN_OPTIONS=suppressions=...; Tests/sanitize.sh sets it, for ASan's leak
# check at exit and for the standalone LSan build). Only third-party code may be listed here - a leak in
# Zamin's own code is a bug to fix. Format: leak:<function, file or library name>.

# miniaudio 0.11.21, PulseAudio backend: when no PulseAudio server answers (CI, containers, xvfb) the failed
# pa_context_connect() path frees the main loop but never pa_context_unref()s the context (miniaudio.h,
# ma_init_pa_mainloop_and_pa_context__pulse) - the context and its memory pool stay allocated.
leak:ma_init_pa_mainloop_and_pa_context__pulse
# miniaudio's JACK backend probe dlopen()s libjack; with no JACK server it is closed again and the objects
# libjack's static constructors made (operator new in dl-init) are left behind.
leak:ma_context_init__jack
# Mesa llvmpipe (Ubuntu 24.04, Mesa 25.2): glGenerateMipmap() on a texture leaves two 56-byte blocks (calloc)
# that the driver never frees - everything else it allocated is freed when the context goes. The driver is
# unloaded at glfwTerminate(), so its own frames cannot be named in the report; the only named frame is the
# one that called GL. OpenGLTexture2D::SetData itself allocates nothing (it only calls glTexSubImage2D /
# glGenerateMipmap), so this cannot hide a leak of ours.
leak:Zamin::OpenGLTexture2D::SetData
# Mesa GLX (Ubuntu 24.04, Mesa 25.2.8-0ubuntu0.24.04.4): the extension-string query
# retains a 128-byte driver allocation after glfwTerminate. CI's complete stack ends
# at GLFW extensionSupportedGLX -> glXQueryExtensionsString; that helper allocates
# nothing itself. Match this vendor query only, never Zamin/GlfwWindow or all of Mesa.
# The local .2 Mesa package does not reproduce it; an intentional application leak
# remains visible with this suppression. Evidence: ASan run 42877104904 artifacts.
leak:extensionSupportedGLX

# Mesa llvmpipe 25.2.8 (.4 Ubuntu CI): primitive-only WorldWorkshop draws retain two
# 56-byte calloc blocks in the driver JIT. Full ASan artifact 42942987405 has 17
# driver frames then OpenGLRendererAPI.cpp:40, the raw glDrawElements call. This
# wrapper only binds a VAO and calls GL; it performs no allocation. The unloaded
# driver frames are misattributed to libZamin by the exit-time symbolizer.
# Match the non-instanced GL call only, never libZamin / Renderer3D generally.
leak:Zamin::OpenGLRendererAPI::DrawIndexed(
